<title>SPAIN: Amper posts 237 pct rise in '96 net profit.</title>
<headline>Amper posts 237 pct rise in '96 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for Spanish telecommunications equipment firm Amper</p>
<p>(in billions of pesetas, unless stated):</p>
<p> Net profit				 9.18    up    237 pct</p>
<p> Ordinary profit			  5.10    up     34 pct</p>
<p> Extraordinary profit		   4.13    vs     n.a.</p>
<p> Sales				     41.34    up	3.23 pct</p>
<p> Cash flow				 17.10    vs	6.39</p>
<p> Financial costs			  1.36    down   41.00 pct</p>
<p> Personnel costs			 10.73    down    4.61 pct</p>
<p> Shareholders equity		   13.56    vs	4.45</p>
<p> Provisions				 4.53    vs	1.70</p>
<p>NOTE - Amper said in a statement its technical services and institutional systems businesses had expanded most during the year, with 44 percent and 19 percent growth respectively.</p>
<p>Among clients, Telefonica sales were most impressive, rising to 25.34 billion pesetas and representing 61.3 percent of total sales.</p>
<p>Amper's cash position exceeded 8.0 billion pesetas at the end of the year.</p>
<p>While its workforce fell by 8.5 percent in 1996 to 1,368 employees, productivity, measured by sales per employee, rose 11.7 percent to exceed 23 million pesetas.</p>
<p>Exports increased by 44.3 percent to 14.57 billion pesetas. The group had sales in 30 countries.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
</text>
